rasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 4; favorites: 2; remixes: 0.\nTags: footer, animated, webgl, threejs, support, flow, effect, navigation.\n## Overview\nNext Gen Footer Section is designed for organizing site-wide navigation, legal links, and utility content. Key features include multi-column navigation groups and clear legal pathways. It is suitable for SaaS websites, product marketing pages, and documentation hubs.\n\nNeural Data Clusters. Adaptive routing algorithms and machine learning endpoints. This is The New Web Distributed consensus protocols shaping the next era of global scale infrastructure. Ledgers. Systems that connect li…\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Neural Data Clusters.; This is The New Web; Ledgers.; 09.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #FF5E3A, secondary #0C0C0C, accent #96F254, background #E2E2E2, surface #A6A07E, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Next-Gen Infrastructure Protocols</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-[#e2e2e2] min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center p-4 md:p-8 font-sans antialiased text-gray-900 selection:bg-black selection:text-white\">\n\n    <main class=\"w-full max-w-[1400px] grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-0 shadow-2xl rounded-sm overflow-hidden\">\n        \n        <!-- Module 1 -->\n        <article class=\"relative h-[600px] md:h-[750px] bg-[#0c0c0c] flex flex-col justify-between p-8 overflow-hidden group\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-module-1\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            \n            <header class=\"relative z-10\">\n                <h2 class=\"text-[#ff5e3a] text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.1]\">Neural<br>Data<br>Clusters.</h2>\n            </header>\n            \n            <footer class=\"relative z-10 flex justify-between items-end text-[#ff5e3a]\">\n                <p class=\"text-xs max-w-[65%] font-medium leading-relaxed\">Adaptive routing algorithms and machine learning endpoints.</p>\n                \n                <div class=\"flex items-center gap-[-2px] shrink-0\">\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#ff5e3a] flex items-center justify-center bg-[#0c0c0c] z-10\"></div>\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-[#ff5e3a] -ml-2\"></div>\n                </div>\n            </footer>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Module 2 -->\n        <article class=\"relative h-[600px] md:h-[750px] bg-[#2d464a] flex flex-col justify-end p-8 overflow-hidden group\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-module-2\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            \n            <div class=\"relative z-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-end w-full\">\n                <h2 class=\"text-[#96f254] text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.1]\">This is<br>The<br>New Web</h2>\n                \n                <div class=\"text-[#96f254] text-xs flex flex-col justify-between h-full gap-6\">\n                    <div class=\"flex items-center gap-[-2px]\">\n                        <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#96f254] flex items-center justify-center bg-[#2d464a] z-10\"></div>\n                        <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-[#96f254] -ml-2\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"font-medium leading-relaxed opacity-90 border-l border-[#96f254]/30 pl-3\">Distributed consensus protocols shaping the next era of global scale infrastructure.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Module 3 -->\n        <article class=\"relative h-[600px] md:h-[750px] bg-[#ff5e3a] flex flex-col justify-between p-8 overflow-hidden group\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-module-3\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            \n            <header class=\"relative z-10\">\n                <h2 class=\"text-[#0c0c0c] text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight\">Ledgers.</h2>\n                <p class=\"text-[#0c0c0c] text-xs font-semibold mt-6 max-w-[85%] leading-relaxed\">Systems that connect liquidity, nodes, and layers into one seamless core ecosystem.</p>\n            </header>\n            \n            <footer class=\"relative z-10 flex flex-col gap-6 text-[#0c0c0c] text-xs font-semibold max-w-[60%] pb-16\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center gap-[-2px]\">\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#0c0c0c] bg-[#0c0c0c] z-10\"></div>\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#0c0c0c] -ml-2 bg-[#ff5e3a]\"></div>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Framework that aligns network endpoints.</p>\n            </footer>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Module 4 -->\n        <article class=\"relative h-[600px] md:h-[750px] bg-[#a6a07e] flex flex-col justify-between p-8 overflow-hidden group\">\n            <canvas id=\"canvas-module-4\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            \n            <header class=\"relative z-10\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center gap-[-2px] mb-8\">\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#0c0c0c] bg-[#0c0c0c] z-10 flex items-center justify-center text-[#a6a07e]\">\n                        <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:code-linear\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"></iconify-icon>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-[#0c0c0c] -ml-2 bg-[#a6a07e]\"></div>\n                </div>\n                <h2 class=\"text-[#0c0c0c] text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-semibold tracking-tighter leading-none\">09</h2>\n                <p class=\"text-[#0c0c0c] text-xs font-semibold mt-6 max-w-[95%] leading-relaxed\">We build foundations that help engineering teams scale effective layer-two strategies.</p>\n            </header>\n            \n            <footer class=\"relative z-10 text-[#0c0c0c] text-xs font-semibold\">\n                <p>Architecting the core logic.</p>\n            </footer>\n        </article>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <script>\n        // Animation Configuration\n        const animate = true;\n        \n        // Utility to setup canvas\n        function setupCanvas(id) {\n            const canvas = document.getElementById(id);\n            const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n            const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n            \n            function resize() {\n                const rect = canvas.parentElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n                canvas.width = rect.width * dpr;\n                canvas.height = rect.height * dpr;\n                ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n            }\n            \n            window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n            resize();\n            return { canvas, ctx, get w() { return canvas.width / dpr }, get h() { return canvas.height / dpr } };\n        }\n\n        // Module 1: Concentric Tunnel\n        const c1 = setupCanvas('canvas-module-1');\n        function drawTunnel(time) {\n            c1.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, c1.w, c1.h);\n            c1.ctx.strokeStyle = '#ff5e3a';\n            c1.ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\n            \n            const numCircles = 35;\n            const maxRadius = Math.max(c1.w, c1.h) * 0.9;\n            const focusX = c1.w * 0.15;\n            const focusY = c1.h * 0.85;\n\n            for (let i = 0; i < numCircles; i++) {\n                let p = (i / numCircles);\n                if (animate) {\n                    p = (p - (time * 0.15)) % 1;\n                    if (p < 0) p += 1;\n                }\n                \n                const radius = maxRadius * Math.pow(p, 1.8);\n                const cx = (c1.w * 0.5) + (focusX - (c1.w * 0.5)) * (1 - p);\n                const cy = (c1.h * 0.4) + (focusY - (c1.h * 0.4)) * (1 - p);\n\n                c1.ctx.beginPath();\n                c1.ctx.arc(cx, cy, Math.max(0, radius), 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                c1.ctx.stroke();\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Module 2: Isometric Mesh\n        const c2 = setupCanvas('canvas-module-2');\n        function drawMesh(time) {\n            c2.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, c2.w, c2.h);\n            c2.ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(150, 242, 84, 0.6)';\n            c2.ctx.fillStyle = '#96f254';\n            c2.ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n\n            const cols = 6;\n            const rows = 14;\n            const cellW = c2.w / (cols - 1);\n            const cellH = c2.h / (rows - 4);\n            \n            const points = [];\n            \n            // Generate points\n            for (let r = -2; r < rows; r++) {\n                const row = [];\n                for (let c = -1; c <= cols; c++) {\n                    let x = c * cellW;\n                    let y = r * cellH;\n                    \n                    // Isometric offset\n                    if (r % 2 !== 0) x += cellW * 0.5;\n                    \n                    // WebGL-style wave animation\n                    if (animate) {\n                        const wave = Math.sin((c * 0.8) + (r * 0.5) + (time * 2)) * 12;\n                        y += wave;\n                    }\n\n                    row.push({x, y});\n                    \n                    // Draw node dots\n                    if (r > 0 && r < rows - 4 && c >= 0 && c < cols) {\n                        c2.ctx.beginPath();\n                        c2.ctx.arc(x, y, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                        c2.ctx.fill();\n                    }\n                }\n                points.push(row);\n            }\n\n            // Draw connecting lines\n            c2.ctx.beginPath();\n            for (let r = 2; r < points.length - 2; r++) {\n                for (let c = 1; c < points[r].length - 1; c++) {\n                    const p = points[r][c];\n                    \n                    // Connect right\n                    if (c < points[r].length - 2) {\n                        c2.ctx.moveTo(p.x, p.y);\n                        c2.ctx.lineTo(points[r][c+1].x, points[r][c+1].y);\n                    }\n                    \n                    // Connect diagonally down\n                    if (r < points.length - 3) {\n                        const downRow = points[r+1];\n                        const cIdx1 = (r % 2 === 0) ? c - 1 : c;\n                        const cIdx2 = (r % 2 === 0) ? c : c + 1;\n                        \n                        if (cIdx1 > 0 && cIdx1 < downRow.length -1) {\n                            c2.ctx.moveTo(p.x, p.y);\n                            c2.ctx.lineTo(downRow[cIdx1].x, downRow[cIdx1].y);\n                        }\n                        if (cIdx2 > 0 && cIdx2 < downRow.length -1) {\n                            c2.ctx.moveTo(p.x, p.y);\n                            c2.ctx.lineTo(downRow[cIdx2].x, downRow[cIdx2].y);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            c2.ctx.stroke();\n        }\n\n        // Module 3: Radiating Beams\n        const c3 = setupCanvas('canvas-module-3');\n        function drawBeams(time) {\n            c3.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, c3.w, c3.h);\n            c3.ctx.strokeStyle = '#0c0c0c';\n            c3.ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\n            \n            const originX = c3.w;\n            const originY = c3.h * 0.5;\n            const numLines = 24;\n            \n            c3.ctx.beginPath();\n            for (let i = 0; i < numLines; i++) {\n                // Spread angles across the left side\n                let angle = (Math.PI * 0.6) + (Math.PI * 0.8 * (i / (numLines - 1)));\n                \n                if (animate) {\n                    const pulse = Math.sin(time * 0.5 + i * 0.2) * 0.05;\n                    angle += pulse;\n                }\n\n                const length = c3.w * 1.5;\n                const endX = originX + Math.cos(angle) * length;\n                const endY = originY + Math.sin(angle) * length;\n\n                c3.ctx.moveTo(originX, originY);\n                c3.ctx.lineTo(endX, endY);\n            }\n            c3.ctx.stroke();\n        }\n\n        // Module 4: Geometric Wedges\n        const c4 = setupCanvas('canvas-module-4');\n        function drawGeometry(time) {\n            c4.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, c4.w, c4.h);\n            c4.ctx.fillStyle = '#111';\n            \n            const size = c4.w * 0.8;\n            const startY = c4.h * 0.6;\n            \n            let offset1 = 0;\n            let offset2 = 0;\n            \n            if (animate) {\n                offset1 = Math.sin(time) * 15;\n                offset2 = Math.cos(time * 0.8) * 15;\n            }\n\n            // Top Triangle\n            c4.ctx.beginPath();\n            c4.ctx.moveTo(c4.w + offset1, startY);\n            c4.ctx.lineTo(c4.w * 0.1 + offset1, startY);\n            c4.ctx.lineTo(c4.w + offset1, startY - size * 0.4);\n            c4.ctx.fill();\n\n            // Bottom Triangle\n            c4.ctx.beginPath();\n            c4.ctx.moveTo(c4.w + offset2, startY + 40);\n            c4.ctx.lineTo(c4.w * 0.1 + offset2, startY + 40 + size * 0.4);\n            c4.ctx.lineTo(c4.w + offset2, startY + 40 + size * 0.4);\n            c4.ctx.fill();\n        }\n\n        // Animation Loop\n        let startTime = Date.now();\n        function render() {\n            const time = (Date.now() - startTime) * 0.001;\n            drawTunnel(time);\n            drawMesh(time);\n            drawBeams(time);\n            drawGeometry(time);\n            requestAnimationFrame(render);\n        }\n        \n        render();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "next-gen-infrastructure-protocols.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/next-gen-infrastructure-protocols.jpg", "source_name": "next-gen-infrastructure-protocols-DESIGN.md", "views": 69, "forks": 7, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-06-12T07:38:10.793894+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T23:33:25.565736+00:00"}